[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:90. What's for Supper]
[00:00.140]Passage 90 | 文章九十
[00:02.130]Brasilia | 巴西利亚
[00:04.240]Though Brazil is one of the richest countries in the world, | 尽管巴西是世界上最富有的国家之一，
[00:08.940]much of it has not yet been developed. | 但其中很大一部分尚未得到开发。
[00:12.290]It was mainly for this reason that the Brazilian government | 主要就是因为这个原因，巴西政府
[00:16.980]decided to have a new city built | 决定在
[00:19.670]600 miles northwest of Rio de Janeiro. | 里约热内卢西北600英里处建造一座新城市。
[00:24.245]Designed by the great architect Lucio Costa, | 由伟大的建筑师卢西奥·科斯塔设计，
[00:28.885]the new city, Brasilia, | 这座新城市，巴西利亚，
[00:31.165]replaced Rio de Janeiro as the capital of Brazil | 于1960年取代里约热内卢成为巴西首都。
[00:36.560]in 1960.
[00:37.545]Brasilia has been carefully planned for modern living. | 巴西利亚经过精心规划，以适应现代生活。
[00:42.370]Its wide roads, which can take 14 lanes of traffic, | 它的宽阔道路可容纳14车道，
[00:47.270]have been kept away from living areas. | 并远离居住区。
[00:50.525]Children do not have to cross busy streets to go to school. | 孩子们上学不必穿过繁忙的街道。
[00:55.670]Housewives can visit shopping centers on foot, | 家庭主妇可以步行前往购物中心，
[00:59.690]for in these specially designed living areas, | 因为在这些特别设计的居住区，
[01:02.970]cars are unnecessary. | 汽车是不必要的。
[01:05.995]At first, the government had great difficulty in persuading people to leave Rio | 起初，政府在说服人们离开里约
[01:12.410]and to settle in Brasilia. | 并定居巴西利亚方面遇到了很大的困难。
[01:14.630]Since 1960, however, | 然而，自1960年以来，
[01:17.515]the population has been growing all the time. | 人口一直在增长。
[01:20.925]Brasilia has quickly established itself as the capital of the country. | 巴西利亚已迅速确立了其作为国家首都的地位。
[01:26.950]The idea to have the capital moved so far inland | 将首都迁至如此内陆地区的想法
[01:32.100]will have a great effect on the future of Brazil. | 将对巴西的未来产生巨大影响。